## 4. Exact Transaction Boundary for Each Write

### ORDER_ACCEPTED (AC1)
```java
@Transactional
OrderSubmissionResponse submit(UUID userId, SubmitOrderRequest request) {
    // ... validations ...
    Order saved = orderRepository.save(order);                           // BEGIN
    statusHistoryRepository.save(orderStatusHistory);                   //
    auditEventWriter.writeOrderAccepted(...);  // ← Audit in transaction //
}                                              // ... COMMIT or ROLLBACK
```
**Boundary:** Same `@Transactional` as order save. Audit rolls back if order save fails.

### PRICE_DECISION (AC2)
```java
@Transactional
void executeOrder(Order order) {
    Quote currentQuote = quoteRepository.findLatestByInstrumentId(...);  // BEGIN
    // ... freshness/tolerance checks ...
    auditEventWriter.writePriceDecision(...);  // ← Audit in transaction
    if (!isPriceWithinTolerance(...)) {
        handlePriceOutOfTolerance(...);                                  //
    } else {                                                             //
        executeFill(...);  // → Nested @Transactional(nested=true)      //
    }
}                                              // ... COMMIT or ROLLBACK
```
**Boundary:** Same `@Transactional` as quote retrieval. PRICE_DECISION commits only if order save commits.

### ORDER_FILLED (AC3)
```java
@Transactional
void executeFill(Order order, Quote quote, BigDecimal executionPrice) {
    Fill fill = new Fill(...);                                          // BEGIN
    fillRepository.save(fill);
    createHoldingMovement(order, fill);                                 //
    createCashTransaction(order, fill, executionPrice);                 //
    applyCashToCache(lockedAccount, ...);                               //
    orderRepository.save(order);  // status → FILLED                    //
    recordStatusHistory(order, "FILLED", ...);                          //
    auditEventWriter.writeOrderFilled(...);  // ← Audit in transaction  //
}                                            // ... COMMIT or ROLLBACK
```
**Boundary:** All ledger writes, cache updates, order status, and status history commit or rollback **together with ORDER_FILLED**. Database trigger on `holding_movements` updates `holdings` cache inside this transaction.

### ORDER_REJECTED (Terminal)
```java
void handlePriceOutOfTolerance(Order order, Quote quote, BigDecimal executionPrice) {
    // ... increment attempts ...
    if (order.getExecutionAttempts() >= MAX_EXECUTION_ATTEMPTS) {       // BEGIN
        order.setStatus("REJECTED");                                    //
        recordStatusHistory(order, "REJECTED", ...);                    //
        auditEventWriter.writeOrderRejected(...);  // ← Terminal event  //
        orderRepository.save(order);                                    //
    }                                              // ... COMMIT or ROLLBACK
    // ...
}
```
**Boundary:** Status, status history, and ORDER_REJECTED audit event commit together. No event if status update rolls back.

### ORDER_REQUEUED (Transient)
```java
void handleStaleQuote(Order order, Quote quote) {
    // ... no status change (stays PENDING) ...
    auditEventWriter.writePriceDecision(...);  // Evidence of stale quote  // BEGIN
    auditEventWriter.writeOrderRequeued(...);  // Retry scheduled           //
    order.setNextExecutionAt(Instant.now().plusSeconds(5));                //
    orderRepository.save(order);                                            //
}                                              // ... COMMIT or ROLLBACK
```
**Boundary:** PRICE_DECISION and ORDER_REQUEUED commit together with order save. If order save fails, both audit events roll back.

